# Path: the stages ahead, to the hardware's speed. Each stage names the evidence that closes it.

n: 7.2
name: stage-1-answers-and-encoding
kind: plan
is: The node encoding is fixed in writing (5.13) with 142 conformance vectors, 93 of them malformed, which the bootstrap's reader holds. Stage 1 closes when a second hand has written a reader from the page alone, in the grammar and kept as nodes (7.13), and the vectors hold in it. The walker reaches a node's parts (5.14.15) and one rule runs as nodes (5.14.18). A reader's rules and print need nothing more; its content id does while that id is SHA-256, which nobody asked for (6.1.31). Who counts as a second hand is question 6.1.30.
status: inferred
from: 5.13 5.2.2 5.3.4 5.1.5 5.11.4 7.13 6.1.30 5.14.15 5.14.18 6.1.31
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.3
name: stage-2-floor
kind: plan
is: The C bootstrap under its budget: the framebuffer, store, canonical reader, walker, page birth and host table. It stands (5.14.10): the ground programs run, a frozen node thaws to the same id, a machine-code leaf runs both unsigned and under the hardened runtime, the build fails over its line count, and a second process records a live run and replays it. It closes when the host functions for symbol lookup, the framework trampoline and threads are written (5.14.9); the clock is.
status: inferred
from: 5.9.1 5.9.2 5.9.3 5.9.4 5.11.4 5.7.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.4
name: stage-3-home-lens
kind: plan
is: The home lens as rows written in the grammar, read forwards and printed backwards. Closes when the lens reads its own definition, prints it, and the reprint reads to the same nodes. A first lens, of words, leaves and six rows written in itself, does that for itself (5.15.3, 5.15.4). Its shapes are brackets only: no pattern over text, no operator table, no named arguments, so the surface of 5.3.5 is not built. Whether the stage is closed by this evidence is the guide's to say.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.2 5.3.5 5.3.3 5.15
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.5
name: stage-4-self-compile
kind: plan
is: The one-pass emitter written in the grammar compiles the compiler. Closes when the system regenerates its own seed byte for byte, cold and compiled runs print the same values over the whole core, and the walker is off the running path after the cold start.
status: inferred
from: 5.10.4 5.10.1 5.10.8 5.9.5 5.10.5
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.6
name: stage-5-control-and-objects
kind: plan
is: Choice with commit, the trail, declared reversibility, the reference pair, composed parents and templates. A cell that holds a node and a trail that a fail unwinds exist (5.14.34); the rest does not. Closes when the thesis example of a class with two parents runs as one composed shape with the view moving on a super-send, a failed option's effects are undone, and each of those tests has been turned red by a planted fault.
status: inferred
from: 5.4.6 5.4.7 5.4.8 5.4.9 5.5.1 5.5.2 5.5.5 5.11.1
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.7
name: stage-6-speed
kind: plan
is: The optimizing tier, then matrix instructions, then the GPU backend. Closes on measurements against optimized C for the same kernels on this machine, with lines of meaning and lines of speed reported apart.
status: inferred
from: 5.10.6 5.10.7 5.10.10
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.8
name: stage-7-lenses
kind: plan
is: A first host-language lens, Go, since NUMS.Go mapped it; then a second; then the first human-language lens. Closes when one program read through two host lenses yields nodes whose shared and differing blueprints are both shown, and the lens declines by name what it cannot print.
status: inferred
from: 5.3.6 5.3.7 6.1.19
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.9
name: stage-8-self-replacement
kind: plan
is: The system writes its own signed executable image and starts from it. Closes when every piece of the C file has a compiled counterpart running in its place and the C file is needed only for a cold start on a new host.
status: inferred
from: 5.9.6 5.9.7
at: 2026-11-24

n: 7.10
name: flows-first
kind: decision
is: The work follows end-to-end flows that really run, watched live through the framebuffer of 5.7.6. Ceremony around the work, the old body's doors, gates, receipts and bands, is left out.
status: given
by: guide
see: 5.7.6
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.11
name: built-with-a-c-compiler-alone
kind: decision
is: This is a new repository and builds with a C compiler alone. The old body appears only as evidence that was read (hubs 2 and 3), never as a tool, a dependency or a step.
status: given
by: guide
see: 5.9.1 2.1
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.12
name: each-stage-closes-on-a-watched-run
kind: plan
is: From stage 3 on, a stage closes on a real run of the thing it adds, recorded from a second process through the framebuffer and replayed, in addition to the evidence its own node names. 'make watch' is the first such run.
status: inferred
from: 7.10 5.7.6 5.11.3
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.13
name: guidance
kind: decision
is: Guidance we hold together, in short form. New code is written in form and kept as nodes; C is the bootstrap only, and no other language is written or stored. Every part can be replaced while the system runs, by a recipe, by machine code, by what comes next. The real work is preferred to a shortcut, and a running flow to a check. Guidance orients and is not enforced: what is aligned needs no permission, and what serves visibility, trust and sovereignty is done.
status: given
by: guide
see: 7.10 7.11 8.14
at: 2026-11-25

n: 7.21
name: every-part-swappable
kind: plan
is: The path to anything being exchanged while it runs. Done: one table says what runs for each operation, each recipe and the step (5.14.19, 5.14.24); an emitter in form compiles a recursion over numbers (5.14.26); the encoding and ice are programs (5.14.32); a watcher in form offers a hot recipe to the emitter while a program runs (5.14.35). Next: emitted code that keeps its values in the walker's own frame, so it can stop at a node it does not know and go on after; then the continuation and undo. After that: bindings from outside through the region, with a scope.
status: inferred
from: 7.13 5.14.19 5.14.23 5.14.24 5.14.26 5.14.35 5.9.6
at: 2026-11-25
